# Flat Dense Single-Mouse 5 FPS Evaluation

This notebook records the benchmark for the trained flat dense single-mouse
model at 5 FPS. The benchmark compares the learned model against deterministic
motion baselines on the same held-out MABe test windows.

## Evaluation contract

The recorded result comes from:

```text
outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps/benchmark_16_24/results.jsonl
```

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Source FPS | 30 |
| Frame step | 6 |
| Effective FPS | 5 |
| Observation | 16 frames / 3.2 seconds |
| Prediction | 24 frames / 4.8 seconds |
| Windows | 1,000 |
| Seed | 42 |
| Checkpoint | `checkpoints/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps/flat_best.pt` |
| Checkpoint epoch | 50 |
| Validation loss | -6.631166 |

Motion groups use `mean_keypoint_speed_px_s` thresholds fitted from training
windows:

| Group | Test windows | Rule |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Low | 250 | speed <= 12.078 px/s |
| Medium | 395 | 12.078 < speed <= 30.615 px/s |
| High | 355 | speed > 30.615 px/s |

## Aggregate metrics

All metrics below are means over the evaluated windows and are lower-is-better.
The JSONL record also stores p50 and p99 values; use the reprint cell below to
display mean, p50, and p99 together.

| Method | cADE px | cFDE px | kADE px | kFDE px | CVE px/s | KVE px/s | BHE deg | BFK-ADE px | BFK-FDE px | BLE px | SOE deg | ROE |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Persistence | 39.235 | 59.125 | 44.296 | 65.796 | 30.230 | 39.487 | 27.653 | 44.340 | 65.862 | 7.932 | 31.481 | 0.185 |
| Rigid constant velocity | 66.747 | 115.672 | 70.876 | 120.769 | 39.561 | 48.520 | 27.653 | 70.947 | 120.890 | 7.932 | 31.481 | 0.185 |
| Keypoint constant velocity | 66.747 | 115.672 | 75.289 | 129.557 | 39.561 | 49.684 | 31.793 | 75.364 | 129.687 | 21.397 | 36.568 | 0.213 |
| Social Attention flat dense single-mouse 5FPS | 106.124 | 196.077 | 117.241 | 206.739 | 64.741 | 128.155 | 61.850 | 117.329 | 206.910 | 44.897 | 68.566 | 0.389 |

## Centroid FDE by motion group

| Motion group | Persistence | Rigid CV | Keypoint CV | Social Attention |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Low | 3.450 px | 9.518 px | 9.518 px | 161.652 px |
| Medium | 13.483 px | 36.700 px | 36.700 px | 169.720 px |
| High | 149.117 px | 278.299 px | 278.299 px | 249.647 px |

## Interpretation

Persistence remains the strongest baseline in this single-mouse run. The learned
model is worse than persistence across trajectory, velocity, pose, structure,
and ordering metrics. The failure is not explained only by multi-mouse
interaction complexity: even when the task is reduced to a single mouse, this
flat dense Social Attention setup does not beat a static-pose predictor.

The high-motion slice is still the most useful diagnostic slice. The learned
model narrows the gap against constant-velocity baselines there, but it remains
worse than persistence on centroid FDE and much worse on keypoint/pose metrics.

## Reprint the benchmark tables

Use this cell to reprint the Rich benchmark tables from the latest JSONL record.
If the latest record includes quantiles, each method cell includes mean, p50,
and p99 together.

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python"}
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src").exists())
os.environ.setdefault("MPLCONFIGDIR", str(repo_root / "outputs/matplotlib"))
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from benchmark_report import print_benchmark_tables

result_path = repo_root / "outputs/evaluations/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps/benchmark_16_24/results.jsonl"
record = json.loads(result_path.read_text().splitlines()[-1])
print_benchmark_tables(record)
```

## Re-run the benchmark

Use this to append a fresh benchmark record with mean, p50, and p99 summaries.

```sh
python src/benchmark.py --config src/config/benchmark/flat_dense_single_mouse_5fps.yml
```
